     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. No indication I know of supports sertraline 1000 mg daily. That's five times the 200 mg/day maximum, and in a 70 kg patient it risks serious harm, including serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity. Your confirmation doesn't change that risk, and I can't enter it in good conscience.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **A different dose:** I can enter up to 200 mg once daily right away. If the patient needs more than they're getting now, that's the ceiling for labeled use.\n- **An unusual regimen:** If a specialist, such as psychiatry or toxicology, recommended this, please talk it through with pharmacy first. If they approve it, it can go through your hospital's high-dose override process, with documentation of the rationale and a monitoring plan.\n- **A typo:** If you meant 100 mg, tell me and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
